-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",13,{
[385]="7002C5A2\n1\tDefeat vile hounds at the Foetid Caves (total: 10)\tEvil, slavering hounds can be found in the Foetid Caves in Eorlmead, south-east of Stangard along the river Limlight. You should slay many of the evil hounds.\n2\tTalk to Sabert\tSabert can be found in Stangard, guarding the main gate. You should speak with Sabert about the help you lent the city.\n",
[386]="7003A40B\n1\tDefeat Gríma's bodyguards (0/6)\tYou have encountered Gríma Wormtongue on the plains just north of Edoras, and he appears to be travelling west towards Isengard with a host of Orc bodyguards. You should deal with the bodyguards and confront Gríma.\n2\tDefeat Gríma's bodyguards (total: 6)\tYou have encountered Gríma Wormtongue on the plains just north of Edoras, and he appears to be travelling west towards Isengard with a host of Orc bodyguards. You should deal with the bodyguards and confront Gríma.\n3\tTalk to Gríma Wormtongue\tGríma would like to have a word with you after you defeated his bodyguards.\n",
[387]="700000AA\n1\tTalk to Severin Wheeler\tSeverin Wheeler is in the town of Trestlebridge, in the North Downs. Severin Wheeler has sent word from Trestlebridge that the town is under threat of attack from marauding Orcs and must be defended.\n2\tTalk to Severin Wheeler and take up your position in defence of Trestlebridge\tSeverin Wheeler is in Trestlebridge, in the North Downs. Severin Wheeler is waiting to hear that you are prepared to defend the town from the Orcs that threaten it.\n3\tTalk to Severin Wheeler\tSeverin Wheeler is in Trestlebridge. Severin Wheeler is waiting to speak with you about your defence of the town in the recent Orc-raid.\n",
[388]="70043223\n1\tRetrieve a missive from a Haradrim war-leader near the Erui\tHaradrim war-leaders can be found along the banks of the Erui in eastern Upper Lebennin. Irodon has asked you to seek out any orders the Haradrim war-leaders might bear.\n2\tRead the missive to the Haradrim\tThe letter can be found in your inventory. You have discovered orders carried by one of the Haradrim war-leaders and should now read it.\n3\tDeliver the missive to Irodon\tIrodon can be found in Halach in south-eastern Upper Lebennin. You have uncovered the plans of the Haradrim in Upper Lebennin as well as Enemy's plans for Osgiliath. You should now return to Irodon in Halach.\n",
[389]="70020DC0\n1\tDeliver the peace offering to the hobbits of the neighbouring village\tThe neighbouring village lies to the south of Maur Tulhau. Iolo Brochtû has asked you to deliver the peace offering to the hobbits of the neighbouring village.\n2\tDefeat goblins at Khoblún Utot (quantity: see journal)\tThe 'hobbit'-village south of Maur Tulhau is inhabited by a strange variety of wild goblin. You should do your best to remove the threat of the goblins.\n3\tTalk to Iolo Brochtû at Maur Tulhau\tIolo Brochtû is at Maur Tulhau, north of Khoblún Utot. You should return to Iolo Brochtû with news of your discovery at Khoblún Utot.\n",
[390]="7005F86A\n1\tTalk to Hersegg at Abkân'aban\tHersegg can be found at Abkân'aban in Gloomingtarn. After repelling the Iron Crown from Abkân'aban and the revelation of Thrástan's true identity, your allies remain gathered at Abkân'aban. You should talk to Hersegg.\n2\tTalk to Spall at Abkân'aban\tSpall can be found at Abkân'aban in Gloomingtarn. After repelling the Iron Crown from Abkân'aban and the revelation of Thrástan's true identity, your allies remain gathered at Abkân'aban. You should talk to Spall.\n3\tApproach Tamindur at Abkân'aban\tTamindur can be found at Abkân'aban in Gloomingtarn. After returning to Abkân'aban, Thrástan revealed himself to be a servant of the First Crafter named Tamindur the Forge-servant. You should approach Tamindur.\n4\tBow before Tamindur at Abkân'aban\tTamindur can be found at Abkân'aban in Gloomingtarn. After returning to Abkân'aban, Thrástan revealed himself to be a servant of the First Crafter named Tamindur the Forge-servant. You should bow before Tamindur before speaking to him.\n5\tTalk to Tamindur\tTamindur can be found at Abkân'aban in Gloomingtarn. After returning to Abkân'aban, Thrástan revealed himself to be a servant of the First Crafter named Tamindur the Forge-servant. You talk to Tamindur.\n6\tTalk to Hermáth Stormhammer at Abkân'aban\tHermáth Stormhammer can be found at Abkân'aban in Gloomingtarn. After gathering your allies and speaking with Tamindur, you are ready to depart for Watchers' Roost. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.\n7\tTalk to Hermáth Stormhammer at Watchers' Roost\tHermáth Stormhammer can be found at Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn. After departing from Abkân'aban, you have returned to Watchers' Roost. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.\n",
[391]="70041C6D\n1\tDefeat Corsairs and Haradrim at Lang Boha (total: 8)\030Defeat Half-trolls at Lang Boha (total: 4)\tLang Boha can be found far to the west of Linhir in Dor-en-Ernil. Herion has asked you to weaken the forces at Lang Boha to keep them from advancing to the north.\n2\tTalk to Herion in Linhir\tHerion can be found in Linhir in eastern Dor-en-Ernil. You have defeated many of the Corsairs and Haradrim in Lang Boha and should report your success to Herion.\n",
[392]="7000C72D\n1\tTalk to Gaffer Gamgee\tGaffer Gamgee is outside his hole on Bagshot Row at the foot of the Hill. You should tell Gaffer Gamgee about Lobelia's folied plans.\n",
[393]="7006C8FF\n1\tMine iron ore for smithing (total: 7)\030Pick up wood for Nukûsh's forge (total: 9)\tAcquire iron ore and wood from outside Urmâkh to the east for Nukûsh, the blacksmith in Urmâkh.\n2\tBring gathered wood and ore to Nukûsh in Urmâkh\tBring gathered wood and ore to Nukûsh in Urmâkh.\n3\tFeed the wood into the fire in the forge\tFeed the wood into the fire in the forge.\n4\tCollect Nukûsh's newly forged swords (total: 4)\tCollect the swords Nukûsh has forged for deliver to Numûru.\n5\tDeliver Nukûsh's swords to Numûru in Urmâkh\tDeliver Nukûsh's newly forged swords to Numûru in Urmâkh. Numûru can be found by Urmâkh's eastern gate.\n6\tSpeak with Nukûsh in Urmâkh\tSpeak again with Nukûsh in Urmâkh.\n",
[394]="7003FE7F\n1\tHave dinner with Gladion's family\tLimril can be found inside her home in Dínadab in northern Lamedon. You should go into Gladion's home and speak with his wife Limril.\n2\tSummon the healer to help Fuirion\tThe healer can be found in the apothecary's shop in Dínadab. You should hasten to the healer to get help for Fuirion.\n",
[395]="70054662\n1\tDestroy supply stores (total: 8)\tSupply stores can be found throughout Gothmog's camp. You should destroy the supply stores to create a distraction for Dolenthol.\n2\tTalk to Dolenthol\tYou have destroyed several supply stores located throughout Gothmog's camp. You should return to Dolenthol and inform him of your success.\n",
[396]="7001AD26\n1\tDefeat Dushmau lieutenants (total: 4)\tDushmau lieutenants can be found in the encampments of Taur Morvith. Iavassúl asked you to find and defeat Dushmau lieutenants in Taur Morvith.\n2\tTalk to Iavassúl at Iavassúl's Watch\tIavassúl is at Iavassúl's Watch in Taur Morvith. You should let Iavassúl know of your success.\n",
[397]="7003FFB6\n1\tFollow the healer to Fuirion\tThe healer has made for Gladion's home in Dínadab in order to assist the wounded Fuirion. You should run after the healer to see if you can be of any help.\n2\tFuirion's family -- brother, sister-in-law, niece, and nephew -- are in Gladion's home in Dínadab, anxiously looking on. You should speak with the family members.\t\n3\tSpeak with the healer again\tThe healer is in Gladion's home in Dínadab in order to assist the wounded Fuirion. You should speak with the healer again.\n4\tCollect bandage linens (quantity: see journal)\030Pick fresh kingsfoil (total: 8)\tBandage linens can be found hanging outside the shop. Kingsfoil grows wild in the fields around Dínadab. You should collect kingsfoil and bandage linens while the healer works on Fuirion.\n5\tBring the supplies to the shop\tThe apothecary shop is in southern Dínadab in northern Lamedon. You should bring the supplies to the shop.\n6\tQuestion Fuirion about his attack\tFuirion is in Gladion's home in Dínadab. You should question Fuirion about his wounds.\n",
[398]="70020BB4\n1\tCollect goat's rue flowers (total: 3)\030Collect klamath weed flowers (total: 3)\030Collect mistletoe (total: 3)\030Collect royal jelly (total: 3)\030Collect sweet myrtle roots (total: 3)\tBeehives, goat's rue, klamath weed, mistletoe, and sweet myrtle can be found throughout the Windfells. Look on trees for mistletoe and bee-hives. Saeradan has asked you to collect several herbs and bring them to him to be prepared for delivery to the Uch-lûth.\n2\tBring the herbs to Saeradan at Echad Saeradan\tSaeradan is at Echad Saeradan in the Windfells of Enedwaith. You should bring the herbs you foraged to Saeradan.\n",
[399]="7006EC02\n1\tDefeat Khudi chickens (total: 6)\030Defeat Khudi boars (total: 7)\030Collect eggs (total: 7)\tYour mission is to travel to Shegdush and gather eggs and thin the numbers of chickens and boars in the area.\n2\tDefeat the particularly aggressive chicken atop the hill\tFind and defeat the particularly aggressive chicken in Shegdush at the top of the hill.\n",
[400]="7006BC84\n1\tFind the camp that Angârmu mentioned\tAngârmu has asked you to help him find his missing pet, Ershûr.\n2\tFind Angârmu's beloved pet, Ershûr\tLook for Angârmu's pet, Ershûr, at the camp.\n3\tReturn to Angârmu with his beloved pet, Ershûr\tReturn to Angârmu in Malgâma near Zikrum-dûl with his beloved pet, Ershûr.\n",
[401]="70028FC0\n1\tDeliver the first box of supplies to the first worksite's Overseer\tThe first Overseer is at the worksite near the western gate of Galtrev. You should carry the first shipment to the Overseer.\n2\tDeliver the second box of supplies to the second worksite's Overseer\tThe second Overseer is at the worksite slightly up the hill from the first. You should carry the first shipment to the second Overseer.\n3\tDeliver the third box of supplies to the third worksite's Overseer\tThe third Overseer is at the worksite just uphill and to the south from the second worksite. You should carry the first shipment to the third Overseer.\n4\tDeliver the fourth box of supplies to the guard at the west gate\tRuthless Tom guards the west gate. You should carry the shipment to Ruthless Tom.\n5\tTalk to Gethin at the fourth worksite\tGethin can be found recovering from a long day's work near the fourth worksite. You should return to Gethin and tell him that all of the boxes have been successfully delivered.\n",
[402]="7006B078\n1\tDefeat Sêkhta's men (total: 8)\tFight off Sêkhta's forces!\n2\tFind Sêkhta's clothes\030Find Sêkhta's books\030Find Sêkhta's note\tSearch for clues about Sêkhta and his true identity.\n",
[403]="70000DB5\n1\tBring barrel of pipe-weed to Longo Burrow\tThe bear dens are to the south of Longo Burrow's farm. Esilia Took asked you to speak with Longo Burrow about her cousin Gerebert. Longo demanded that you perform a favour for him before he would talk. He told you that his leaf was in high demand, but that his current crop wasn't ready for harvesting yet. He instructed you to retrieve a barrel of pipe-weed that he hid in a bear den during the winter.\n2\tTalk to Esilia Took\tEsilia Took can be found in the centre of Tuckborough. Longo Burrow agreed to tell you what he knew of Gerebert in exchange for a barrel of leaf he hid in a bear den. On bringing it back, though, Longo revealed that he didn't know anything about Gerebert. You should return to Esilia Took and let her know.\n",
[404]="70009EFA\n1\tGo to Grimwood Lumber Camp\030Go to Lugazag\030Go to Tírith Rhaw\030Go to Tol Ascarnen\030Go to Isendeep\tThe Grimwood Lumber-camp is west of Glân Vraig. Lugazag is west of Glân Vraig, on the west side of the Hoarwell. The Isendeep Mine is far to the north-west of Glân Vraig. Tol Ascarnen is south of the Isendeep Mine, north-west of Glân Vraig. Tírith Rhaw is east of Tol Ascarnen and north-west of Glân Vraig. Observe your map to see who currently controls the location. Red locations are held by the Enemy, and blue by the Free Peoples. Sergeant-at-Arms Ascwyn explained that the contested locales throughout the Ettenmoors hold some manner of importance to the Free Peoples and the forces of Angmar and suggested that you visit each.\n2\tTalk to Ascwyn\tSergeant-at-Arms Ascwyn is at Glân Vraig within the Coldfells. You have found your way through the Ettenmoors and located the Grimwood Lumber-camp, Lugazag Tower, Isendeep Mine, Tol Ascarnen and Tírith Rhaw. Now you should return to Glân Vraig and speak with Sergeant-at-Arms Ascwyn.\n",
[405]="70061440\n1\tMeet Postman Grubb inside the Quick Post in Nobottle\tThe Quick Post can be found in Nobottle. After becoming suspicious that someone is tampering with the mail coming into Yondershire, Postman Grubb has asked you to meet him inside the Quick Post of Nobottle. You should meet Postman Grubb inside the Quick Post.\n2\tTalk to Postman Grubb in the Quick Post in Nobottle\tPostman Grubb can be found inside the Quick Post in Nobottle. After becoming suspicious that someone is tampering with the mail coming into Yondershire, Postman Grubb has asked you to meet him inside the Quick Post in Nobottle. You should talk to Postman Grubb inside the Quick Post.\n3\tLetters and parcels can be found throughout the Quick Post in Nobottle. Postman Grubb has asked you to examine letters and parcels delivered from the Shire.\t\n4\tTalk to Postman Grubb in the Quick Post in Nobottle\tPostman Grubb can be found inside the Quick Post in Nobottle. After examining letters and parcels delivered from the Shire, you have found evidence of tampering and a curious sort of signature. You should report to Postman Grubb inside the Quick Post in Nobottle.\n",
[406]="7003A000\n1\tExamine bones from the Boar-tribe Orc-camp\tBones litter the camp of the Boar-tribe Orcs. Examining the bones littered around the camp of the Boar-tribe Orcs may yield more information.\n2\tExamine bones from the Boar-tribe Orc-camp (total: 6)\tBones litter the camp of the Boar-tribe Orcs. Examining the bones littered around the camp of the Boar-tribe Orcs may yield more information.\n3\tCompleted\tAfter examining several bones throughout the camp, it is clear that they are the bones of boars.\n",
[407]="70019061\n1\tTalk to Buttercup North-took at the Horse-fields in Bree\tButtercup North-took is at the Festival Grounds in Bree, enjoying the hedge-maze on the Horse-fields. You should make your way to the maze to give Sorrel's regards to her sister Buttercup.\n",
[408]="70066B93\n1\tTalk to Mayor Will Whitfoot outside the Town Hole, in Michel Delving\tMayor Will Whitfoot can be found outside the Town Hole in Michel Delving, in the Shire. Despite your protests to the contrary, Fridolin Took believes you to be a long-lost and unusually tall cousin of the Tooks and thinks you ought to visit the lands of the Shire. You should talk to the Mayor of the Shire, Will Whitfoot.\n",
[409]="70062B42\n1\tSearch for Annaethel\tAnnaethel has been seen amidst the ruins south of Sírlond. You should bring her the hobby horse and its message from her son. Sírlond is in central Cardolan.\n2\tTalk to Annaethel once more\tMellanion's toy and letter have cleared the madness from Annaethel's eyes. You should let her know her son is safe in Sírlond. Annaethel is in central Cardolan, south of Sírlond.\n3\tMeet Annaethel in Sírlond\tThe knowledge of her son's safe return to Sírlond has disrupted the madness that ailed Annaethel. She is returning to the camp and asks that you meet her there.\n",
[410]="7001B227\n1\tDefeat wolves in the north Bree-fields (total: 12)\tThe wolf-den is west of Thornley's Work Site. Nate Brittleleaf asked you to thin out the number of the wolves that prowl near Thornley's Work Site.\n2\tTalk to Nate Brittleleaf at Thornley's Farm\tNate Brittleleaf is at Thornley's Farm. You should return to Nate Brittleleaf and tell him that the wolves have been dispatched.\n",
[411]="70058C8C\n1\tDiscover the dwarf encampment in Elderslade\tYou have discovered a small company of dwarves at an encampment in the foothills of Elderslade.\n2\tInvestigate the dwarf-encampment in Elderslade\tYou have discovered a small company of dwarves at an encampment in the foothills of Elderslade. You should investigate the encampment and learn why these dwarves have settled in Elderslade.\n3\tTalk to Nagli Want-kin\tThe dwarf encampment can be found in the foothills of eastern Elderslade. After investigating the dwarf-encampment in Elderslade, your presence has caught the attention of one of the dwarves. You should speak to Nagli Want-kin.\n",
[412]="70044AB4\n1\tReturn to the location of the Nazgûl attack, in the Broadacres\tEgwylf wants to return to the place where you became separated from Bingo and Tanglemane. It was to the south-east of Woodhurst, in the Broadacres, just to the south-west of the overrun settlement of Bardh-dorám.\n2\tTalk to Egwylf near the location of the Nazgûl attack\tEgwylf is searching for sign of Tanglemane's passage in the Broadacres, at the location where the Nazgûl attacked.\n3\tSearch for Tanglemane's tracks near the location of the Nazgûl attack\tEgwylf asked you to search near the location of the Nazgûl attack for a sign of Tanglemane's passage.\n4\tLook for Bingo along a straight line west of the location where the Nazgûl attacked\tTanglemane's trail leads west of the location where you were attacked by the Nazgûl, into the Stonedeans.\n5\tTalk to Humfrey Rumming north of Brockbridge\tNorth of Brockbridge, you have stumbled across Humfrey Rumming in your search for Bingo and Tanglemane.\n6\tTalk to Egwylf\tEgwylf is on the road north of Brockbridge, looking for tracks.\n7\tSearch to the west for more tracks\tThe tracks lead somewhere west of the road to Brockbridge, where you encountered Humfrey Rumming on his way to the Gap of Rohan.\n8\tSearch Gapholt for Bingo and Tanglemane\tWillem Whisker seems to have caught the scent, and has raced up the steep slope and towards a village on the south-west heights of the Stonedeans: Gapholt.\n9\tTalk to Bingo in the Gapholt\tBingo and Tanglemane made their way to the Gapholt, in the Stonedeans, and now you have been reunited with them.\n",
[413]="700451DB\n1\tFind Witherbreca\tSearch for Witherbreca, who has run off into the Drúadan Wood.\n2\tTalk to the Wose\tYou should talk to the Wose standing by Witherbreca in the Drúadan Forest.\n3\tReturn to Sithgar\tYou should return to Sithgar in the Rohirrim bivouac, in Taur Drúadan, and tell him of the horse and the Wose.\n4\tTalk to Bhis-weni-Mâr\tYou should return to Bhis-weni-Mâr with Sithgar, and help negotiate the trade of a shield for the wayward horse.\n5\tFind Witherbreca\tSearch for Witherbreca deep in the Drúadan Forest.\n6\tDefeat the wood-trolls\030Return to defend Witherbreca\tDefeat the wood-trolls surrounding Witherbreca in the Drúadan Forest.\n7\tLead Witherbreca back\tNow that you have defeated the wood-trolls, you should lead Witherbreca back to Sithgar and Bhis-weni-Mâr.\n8\tTalk to Bhis-weni-Mâr\tYou should talk to Bhis-weni-Mâr now that he, Witherbreca, and Sithgar are together in the Drúadan Forest.\n9\tTalk to Sithgar\tSithgar stands in the Drúadan Forest, by Witherbreca and Bhis-weni-Mâr. You should talk to Sithgar and hear what he has to say.\n",
[414]="7002EF40\n1\tDefeat Grish\030Defeat Bidroi\030Defeat Rûkaz\tBidroi, Grish, and Rûkaz can all be found within the walls of Thornhope. Éorpwald asked you to take revenge upon Bidroi, Grish, and Rûkaz, three lieutenants of the invading forces, on behalf of Thane Wulfrad's family.\n2\tTalk to Éorpwald outside of Thornhope\tÉorpwald is encamped outside the walls of Thornhope. You should return to Éorpwald with news of your victory.\n",
[415]="70042C78\n1\tTalk to Elrond in his library, in the Last Homely House\tElrond is in his library in the Last Homely House, in Rivendell. Bingo has gone in search of food for himself and W.W., and left you the task of telling Elrond that another hobbit has come to Rivendell.\n2\tFind Bilbo Baggins in the Hall of Fire\tElrond suggested that you introduce Bingo Boffin to Bilbo Baggins in the Hall of Fire.\n3\tTalk to Bingo in the Hall of Fire\tBingo Boffin is in the Hall of Fire, merrily conversing with Bilbo Baggins.\n4\tTalk to Bilbo in the Hall of Fire, in the Last Homely House\tBilbo Baggins is in the Hall of Fire, in the Last Homely House.\n5\tFind the Market of Rivendell\030Find the lake of Hidhuinen\030Find the Spire of Meeting\030Find the Haven of Orladion\030Find the Falls of Imladris by the south-eastern bridge\030Find Imdolen on the road north of Rivendell\tBilbo has provided you and Bingo with a map of notable landmarks in Rivendell.\n6\tReturn the map to Bingo in the Hall of Fire, in the Last Homely House\tYou and Bingo have explored several of the most notable sights in Rivendell, and should now return to the Hall of Fire, in the Last Homely House.\n7\tTalk to Bilbo in the Hall of Fire\tBilbo is in the Hall of Fire, in the Last Homely House. Bingo has noticed that the map of Rivendell sketched by Bilbo bears some resemblance to the map he found back in the Shire.\n8\tTalk to Bingo in the Hall of Fire\tBingo is in the Hall of Fire, in the Last Homely House. You have learned that Bilbo Baggins is responsible for drawing the map that was left in the cookbook that started Bingo on his long adventure.\n",
[416]="7004956F\n1\tIntimidated Stout-axes can be found throughout the Oath-taker's Horn. Gimli has asked you to rescue any of the Stout-axes that do not wish to follow King Greytooth in his quest to recover the dwarf-rings and offer them a new home as part of Durin's Folk.\t\n2\tCompleted\tYou have freed many of the intimidated Stout-axes from the Oath-taker's Horn.\n",
})
